From 7845d591f8910f2ac411b5d0d94ee1d5c5a687a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:10:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Turn the audit log into a calendar-based daily weather
 history

- Month calendar (weeks, Sunday first) with prev/next, month picker and
  Today; today outlined, days with records marked by their worst decision
  and record count.
- Clicking a day opens that day's record: 5 ft / 30 ft high-low, wind range
  and prevailing direction, humidity, largest inversion and shear, hidden
  risks, conditions, pesticide, treatment, sources, then that day's rows in
  the existing audit table. Days without records say so; nothing is
  estimated. Precipitation is shown as not recorded (no sensor for it).
- Records are filed by observation date in the zone stored with each record,
  so days never mix; existing records are kept and filed by their own dates.
- Duplicates: an observation with the same data and timestamp is stored once
  (append returns the existing record); identical copies saved earlier by
  the 15-second heartbeat are shown once. Storage is unchanged otherwise.
- Export / printable report scope: selected day, ticked days, month, or all
  history. CSV keeps its columns and adds Observation date.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
